2. villa, Vesuvius Challenge (MIT), commit 0fb38c45
   https://github.com/ScrollPrize/villa

   Covers: the Rust ports of villa's ink inference (vesuvius/src/vesuvius/ink_detection):
   - src/model.rs, inkrs-kernels/src/stem.rs, inkrs-kernels/src/inorm.rs, inkrs-kernels/src/layout.rs:
     the Local3DStem2DUNet network and its LocalDepthFusionStem, layer for layer, under PyTorch's FP16
     autocast semantics
   - src/sched.rs, inkrs-kernels/src/blend.rs: infer.py's tile positions (_sliding_positions_1d,
     iter_blocks), its empty-tile skips and occupancy-level choice, the floored Hann blend window,
     the accumulation order and the uint8 finish
   - inkrs-kernels/src/tiles.rs: normalize_robust
   - src/zarr.rs, src/main.rs: the input level, layer selection and output naming villa uses
   The scripts p0_torch.py, export_weights.py and villa_coverage.py import villa at run time to build
   references; they do not copy its code.

