3. NVIDIA libdevice (CUDA Toolkit 13.2, NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit End User License Agreement)

   Covers: ptx/inkrs.sm80.ptx and ptx/inkrs.sm120.ptx. scripts/build-ptx.sh links libdevice.10.bc
   (its SHA-256 is in ptx/tools.txt) into the kernels of both, so the PTX contains compiled code from
   libdevice's __nv_dsqrt_rn, __nv_expf, __nv_sqrtf, __nv_fmaxf, __nv_fminf, __nv_logf, __nv_rintf and __nv_rsqrtf.
   libdevice is listed as distributable in Attachment A of the CUDA EULA, and that code is
   distributed under the EULA's terms, not under inkrs's licence. The EULA is at
   https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/ and in each CUDA Toolkit as EULA.txt.

